+## Access
+
+Every request carries an API key: `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are
+stored in the data as `apiKeys: [{ "key", "name", "role" }]`.
+
+- No key, or a key that is not known: `401` with code `unauthorized`.
+- A known key whose role may not use the route: `403` with code `forbidden`.
+
+Roles:
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: what a viewer may, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that may change data (any method but `GET`) made with a known
+key writes an audit entry `{ id, at, keyName, method, path, status }`, also
+when it is refused or fails. `GET /audit` lists the entries newest first and
+is for managers only.
+
